      "attributes": {
        "id": 1392,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both 各 and それぞれ express the idea of 'each' or 'every', but they differ in usage. 各 always goes before a noun, for example, 各部屋 'each room', 各階 'each floor', and so on. それぞれ, on the other hand, can stand alone at the start of a sentence or be attached to a noun with の. For example, 人はそれぞれ違う意見がある ('People each have differing opinions.').",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 652,
          "slug": "各",
          "title": "各",
          "meaning": "Each, Every, Respective, Various",
